    {
      "id": "dg0ft57",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.3 Climate"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Telangana has a tropical climate characterized by hot summers, a monsoon season, and mild winters. The climate is semi-arid in many districts.",
      "id": "mvfjfye"
    },
    {
      "id": "obs67xa",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Season</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Months</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Characteristics</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Summer</p>",
            "<p>March to June</p>",
            "<p>Very hot; temperatures up to 45°C; Hyderabad averages 40°C</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Southwest Monsoon</p>",
            "<p>June to September</p>",
            "<p>Main rainy season; avg rainfall 900mm</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Northeast Monsoon</p>",
            "<p>October–November</p>",
            "<p>Some rain in south Telangana</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Winter</p>",
            "<p>December to February</p>",
            "<p>Mild and pleasant; 15°C to 25°C</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "63hinpq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.4 Forests and Wildlife"
    },
    {
      "id": "y8q0722",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2.4.1 Forest Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Telangana has about 24,738 sq km of forest cover (about 22% of its area). Major forest types include tropical dry deciduous forests, tropical moist deciduous forests, and scrub forests.",
      "id": "5dd6g4e"
    },
    {
